    "description": "is_pii means personally identifiable information about a natural person. Judge each Attribute on its own meaning: documented, or plain from its name in its table. Set true when it identifies, contacts or locates an identifiable person, or holds a sensitive personal detail: personal names; a person's email, phone or address, business or private; government identifiers; identifiers whose values each point to one person, such as employee or contact numbers; date of birth; and person-linked medical or financial details. Set false when its meaning is non-personal, such as product codes, quantities, statuses, business dates, load timestamps, or company identifiers and names. Data type, uniqueness, key membership or a previous true finding alone does not establish PII. Set null only when the Attribute's meaning is unknown or the evidence conflicts. Never copy one finding across all columns. is_masking_required is separate and never changes. Never expose example personal values."
